D.Mont L.R. 83.8 Self-Represented Litigants
(A) Where the client is the United States, the consent of the United
States Attorney for the District of Montana is required;
(B) Where the client is the State of Montana, the consent of the
Attorney General is required;
(2) file Form M in the record of the case, attaching Forms J, K, and L;
(3) assist and counsel the student and accept full personal and
professional responsibility for all work performed by the student;
(4) ensure that at least one supervising attorney:
(A) is present in person throughout the student’s presentations in
open court;
(B) signs all written submissions in which the student participates
and briefly notes the student’s participation; and
(5) at the student’s first presentation in open court, introduce the student
to the presiding judge.
